<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Entangle</h1>
<p>Sphere: Creation Sphere
Class: Druid (guild level 21, up to 80%), Ranger (guild level 35, up to 50%)
Mana: 30
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cast entangle &lt;target&gt;
</pre>
<p>The caster raises both hands slowly and points, and thick, writhing vines 
shoot from the ground and wrap the target. Held in the vines, they can do 
little but look about, talk and check themselves; they can't walk away, and 
a player can cast no spell but dispel magic. Nobody can hit or attack them 
while they are bound, but spells still reach them, and a fight already 
going on carries on. The vines hold for about half a minute, a little 
longer the better your spell, and a strong enough dispel magic tears them 
away.
</p><p>The target resists with their mind, against your mind and your skill in 
the spell. The vines won't take hold of anyone above level 50, and they 
only grow in fields, forests, hills, swamps and cities. Whether or not 
the vines take hold, casting it makes the target attack you. It can be 
cast while fighting. Practising it needs divine 70. It is also found on 
potions, wands and scrolls.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
